    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36407" root="قوس" body-key="q">
    
      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تقوّس</span></b>  <i>It</i> (a thing) <i>became bowed,</i> or <i>bent;</i>
as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استقوس</span></b> : (TA:) the ↓ latter is also said,
tropically, of the moon when near the change
[&amp;c.]. (A, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  (tropical:)  <i>He</i> (an old man, S, A)
<i>became bowed,</i> or <i>bent;</i> (A, * K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوَّسَ</span></b> ,
inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَقْوِيسٌ</span>; (S, A, * Msb, K;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استقوس</span></b> ;
(S;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اقوس</span></b> : (A:) or <i>he became bowed,</i> or
<i>bent, in the back;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوَّسَ</span></b> ; and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استقوس</span></b> ;
(TA;) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوِسَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوَسَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوَسٌ</span>. (K.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تقوّس قَوْسَهُ</span> <i>He put his bow upon his back.</i>
(TA.)

